WEBVTT

NOTE Edited transcription of a historical recording. Unclear speech is marked; use current specifications for ordering.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.200
Welcome, and thank you for joining today's
session on standard cabinet modifications

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:08.200
in Eclipse Cabinetry.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:14.300
Whether you're designing a kitchen, bathroom, or
custom space, Eclipse offers flexible options

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.800
to tailor cabinets to your exact needs.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:20.200
Let's explore how these modifications work.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:25.100
First, understanding standard modifications.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:29.700
While Eclipse Cabinetry offers a variety of
standard cabinet modifications, not every

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:32.500
cabinet can be modified in the same way.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:37.500
It's important to first review the cabinet
specifications in the spec book before checking

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:45.100
the modifications options on pages C1 and C2 of
the spec book.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:49.100
Take this example of this three-drawer base
cabinet.

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:55.500
It can be modified in width, height, and depth,
but some limitations still apply.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:05.200
Always verify what is and isn't possible for
each specific cabinet before proceeding.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:11.700
With toe kick modifications, you can change the
toe kick of a base cabinet or a tall cabinet

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:14.400
for functional or aesthetic reasons.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:16.900
The standard toe kick is four inches high

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:19.500
and is recessed three inches deep

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:21.600
on the front of each cabinet.

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:25.200
But you can also request a removable toe kick,

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:29.100
RMK at $146 per cabinet,

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:32.500
which is especially useful for installing tall
cabinets.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:38.400
You can also request a flush toe kick, FTK at
$89 per cabinet

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:41.400
where there is no recess space.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:45.600
You can request a no-toe kick NTK,

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:48.500
which is also $89 per cabinet,

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:51.300
which removes the toe kick sub-base completely.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:53.500
Please note that the overall height of this
cabinet

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:56.500
will be reduced by four inches.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:59.700
And lastly, you can also choose a custom toe
kick

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:01.600
that's recessed on the side,

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:06.100
the left side, the right side, or the back, or
all three.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:09.500
And note that you can actually do all three
recessed

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:12.800
for one $146 cabinet charge.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:20.300
You can also do a modification of full height
doors.

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:23.900
This is FHD and it's actually no charge.

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:26.600
So most base cabinets that come with a top
drawer

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:28.800
can be modified to have full height doors

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:30.400
at no extra charge.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.100
This is a common modification

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:35.000
in vanity and blind corner bases especially.

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:44.800
Along with maybe choosing to do a full height
door in a blind corner cabinet,

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:47.700
you also need to note that you can also fill the
blind area.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:51.700
The standard way that a blind corner cabinet
will come

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:55.100
is actually an open area on the blind side.

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:57.100
So if you'd like to have this space built in,

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:03.800
choose FBBA for a fill blind base cabinet at
$232,

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:10.800
or you can choose F-WBA for wall cabinets at
$146 per cabinet.

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:20.800
By default, adjustable shelves in base cabinets
and in the top section of tall cabinets are
always half depth.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:26.800
You can upgrade to full depth shelves, FDS, for
$89 per cabinet.

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:43.800
For custom height rollout trays, you can also
change the height of a rollout. Standard
rollouts are 3 inches high. With a CROT
modification, you can request either a 4 inch or
a 7 inch height.

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:50.800
Please keep in mind that the usable space of
this rollout will always be about 3 quarter
inches less than the stated height.

00:03:50.800 --> 00:04:04.800
For a finished interior, F.I., you can choose to
match the interior of the cabinet with a door
color for an additional 25% upcharge.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:14.800
Please note that this will only include the
interior sides, tops, bottoms, backs, and the
adjustable shelves for that price.

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:19.800
Any interior drawers, rollouts, or accessories
will not be finished to match.

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:30.800
For custom sizing, most of our cabinets can be
adjusted in width, height, and depth using
eighth-inch increments.

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:36.800
The most common would be for a standard square
cabinet, meaning that the front is not angled.

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:46.300
Your choices are going to be MOD SQ30 or MOD
SQ50.

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:52.500
For the MOD SQ30, reductions in size within six
inches of the normal size are 30%

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:53.500
upcharge.

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:59.900
For the MOD SQ50, this would be for increases in
size or changes beyond six inches,

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:03.000
and that would be a 50% upcharge.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:07.600
Please note that you should always check the
spec book page on the cabinet you'd like to

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:09.200
modify first.

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:14.800
Some cabinets can't be resized in every
direction.

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:18.000
And there are some no charge exceptions.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:23.100
In the eclipse cabinet line, up to 30% of the
cabinets in your order can be reduced

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:26.000
in width at no extra charge.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:31.100
Beyond that though, the usual 30% or 50%
upcharge applies.

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:35.600
should be done in 1/8-inch increments based on
the next standard size. For example, if

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:40.800
you order 10 cabinets and would like to reduce
the width of 4 of them, 3 of them will be

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:46.700
at no charge, while the 4th will have the 30%
upcharge. You can also choose standard

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:52.500
depth modifications. Many cabinets are available
in multiple depths, and this might include

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:59.100
13 inches, 16 inches, 18, 21, or 24 inches in
depth.

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:02.000
However, you must check the spec book.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:05.000
And if that size is not listed in the spec book,

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:07.700
a custom charge will still apply.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:09.500
In our three drawer base cabinet example

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:11.500
we had looked at previously, you can

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:15.300
see that the spec book shows that it is
available in 13, 16,

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:19.300
18, and 21 inches deep at the standard price.

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:21.400
This cabinet normally would be at 24,

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:24.200
so it also includes the 24 inch depth.

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:26.300
But note that there also are some restrictions

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:30.100
over size based on width and also in depth.

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:31.500
So keep that in mind.

00:06:34.600 --> 00:06:38.300
For angled cabinets, the modification to change

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:42.700
the height, the width, or the depth is mod ang.

00:06:42.700 --> 00:06:46.500
This will include a 50% upcharge for size
reductions

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:48.800
in width, height, and depth, or for changes

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:52.000
that are less than six inches from the standard
size.

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:54.900
For any increases in size or changes that are
greater

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:58.800
than six inches in difference, please submit a
custom quote

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:01.300
to quotes@wwinc.com.

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:07.100
To add a beaded back panel to a cabinet,

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:12.100
you can choose this with most of our cabinets.

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:16.600
Please note that this also needs to be selected

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:19.700
only with our finished interior selection.

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:23.300
These are also not compatible with TFL, HPL,

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:24.800
or acrylic finishes.

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:31.200
If you need to ship a door loose or a door front
loose,

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:32.900
and this might be for a reason,

00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:37.100
such as you want to turn a cabinet into a sink
base,

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:39.800
or perhaps you have a tall pantry cabinet

00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:41.800
and you want to have a door ship loose

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:45.500
so it can be, an accessory can be added to that
cabinet

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:49.100
after the fact and you don't want it drilled for
hinges,

00:07:49.100 --> 00:07:51.700
you can specify a loose door or drawer front.

00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:56.700
For each loose door drawer front though,

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:59.500
it would be a $100 list charge.

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:02.400
You need to specify which of those fronts you'd
like loose

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:05.200
and also whether or not you'd like them bored
for hinges.

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:09.600
Another fun modification that we offer

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:12.500
is a plumbing access drawer.

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:14.900
And this would be often used in a three drawer

00:08:14.900 --> 00:08:17.400
or a two drawer cabinet where you're going to be
using it

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:19.600
as a sink base and would like to have access

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:21.500
for the plumbing.

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:24.400
For the wood dovetail drawer box,

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:27.700
we call those PAD, plumbing access drawer.

00:08:27.700 --> 00:08:30.200
And what this will give you is a notch.

00:08:30.200 --> 00:08:33.300
So the notch would be 11 and seven eighths deep

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:35.400
and it's available in three different widths,

00:08:35.400 --> 00:08:38.400
four inches, six inches or eight inches.

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:40.700
Please note that these are only available in
cabinets

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:44.000
that are 24 to 42 inches wide only.

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:47.700
So anything smaller than 24 or wider than 42

00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:49.900
will not be able to have a notch drawer.

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:54.200
These are also only available in cabins

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:56.500
that are at least 18 inches deep.

00:08:56.500 --> 00:08:58.500
And the drawer box itself must be

00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:00.400
one of our standard drawer box heights,

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:01.900
which would include three inches,

00:09:01.900 --> 00:09:04.100
four inches, or seven inches high.

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:09.900
You can also do a plumbing access area

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:13.500
for a simulated metal plumbing drawer box.

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:17.100
In this case, the code is going to be SMPDD,

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:19.700
and it's at $130 list.

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:22.200
This actually creates a full void

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:23.900
all the way from the back of the drawer

00:09:23.900 --> 00:09:26.400
to the front of the drawer face.

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:30.300
And so not just a notch, but rather a divided
drawer.

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:32.900
And so you are seeing the difference in the
change here.

00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:34.400
Just like the other ones though,

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:36.000
these are only available in cabinets

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:38.500
that are 24 to 42 inches wide

00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:40.000
and not available in cabinets

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:41.900
that are less than 18 inches deep.

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:49.700
And lastly, you can also get a divided drawer
for a Legrabox metal drawer box.

00:09:49.700 --> 00:09:53.200
These are the Blum Legrabox metal drawer boxes.

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:58.200
And so in this case, again, your choice for the
divided section where that void is in

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:04.100
the center would be the void of four inches
wide, six inches, or eight inches wide.

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:08.900
Again, only available in cabinets that are 24 to
42 inches wide and not available in

00:10:08.900 --> 00:10:16.600
cabinets that are less than 18 inches deep. For
a full handle-less look, you can

00:10:16.600 --> 00:10:23.300
also choose touch latches or tip-on hardware.
These will allow you to open

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:27.600
doors and drawers with just a gentle push, but
please note that if you add

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:32.800
this to your cabinet, the way that the door and
drawer opens is by touching the

00:10:32.800 --> 00:10:38.200
door and drawer. Over time, this might wear down
the finish, and any issues that

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:41.000
may develop over time with that repeated contact

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:43.100
will not be covered under warranty.

00:10:45.800 --> 00:10:49.800
The last modification in our standard
modifications

00:10:49.800 --> 00:10:52.800
is actually on page C2 at the very top.

00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:56.000
And this is the extended side to the floor.

00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:59.400
This is a modification for base cabinets and
tall cabinets.

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:02.400
You still would have the recessed toe kick in
the front,

00:11:02.400 --> 00:11:05.500
but the side of the cabinet would extend to the
floor

00:11:05.500 --> 00:11:10.200
and not have that exposed notched area on that
side.

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:12.800
For an extended right side to the floor,

00:11:12.800 --> 00:11:14.800
use code ESFR.

00:11:14.800 --> 00:11:18.400
For extended left side of the floor, use ESFL.

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:23.000
For extending both sides to the floor, use ESFB.

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:26.300
And this will be $89 per side.

00:11:26.300 --> 00:11:29.000
So please note if you choose that ESFB,

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:30.900
you do need to double that price.

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:40.200
This concludes the whole training on our
standard cabinet modifications.

00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:47.000
For any questions, please refer to the ECLP spec
book for any cabinet specific options.

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:51.300
For any special requests that are not included
within these standard modifications, please

00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:55.370
email to quotes@wwinc.com.
